Package: pcountr
Title: Interactive Stratigraphic Grain Counter with PCount Legacy Support
Version: 0.5.2
Authors@R:
    person("William", "Nanavati",
           email   = "william.nanavati@umontana.edu",
           role    = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4853-5429"))
Description: An interactive, keystroke-driven counting application for recording
    stratigraphic assemblages at the microscope — pollen, diatoms, charcoal
    morphotypes, or any proxy counted by traversing a slide. Counts are saved
    continuously to a self-contained YAML format carrying identifications, metadata, depth,
    and age. Provides report calculations (assemblage sums, tracer-spike ratios,
    concentrations, traverse statistics, preservation tabulations), a wide
    samples-by-taxa matrix for stratigraphic plotting (e.g. 'rioja'), accumulation
    rates, and export to Tilia XML (.tlx) for Neotoma integration and upload. Also reads and
    converts legacy MS-DOS 'PCount' .CNT files and their .DIC dictionaries.
    Chronology construction is delegated to dedicated tools (e.g. 'rbacon',
    'clam'); pcountr performs accumulation-rate arithmetic from
    analyst-supplied ages. Dedicated to the memory of Dr. Eric C. Grimm
    (1951--2020), who developed PCount at the Illinois State Museum and trained
    generations of palynologists in its use.
